[38;5;231m⏺[39m I've opened three layout sketches in a browser tab:
  [94m]8;id=117igo6;http://localhost:49296/?key=d4c2b1a36009784b742708f1ae48a2267f321f472349d9cd5da94500f58cbf94\http://localhost:49296/?key=d4c2b1a36009784b742708f1ae48a2267f321f472349d9cd5da94500f58cbf94[39m]8;;\. The tab uses a lot of
  tokens, so tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal.

  All three use the same four groups: [1mProfile[0m (name, email, avatar URL), [1mPreferences[0m (time zone, language, theme),
  [1mNotifications[0m (email, push, weekly digest) and [1mSecurity[0m (2FA, session timeout, API token). There's still one Save
  button in each.

  - [1mA. Stacked sections (my recommendation):[0m one scrolling page, with a heading for each group and lines between groups.
    It's the smallest change, needs no JavaScript, and keeps every field visible.
  - [1mB. Card per group:[0m the same page, but each group sits in its own bordered box, so the groups stand apart more
    clearly.
  - [1mC. Sidebar or tabs:[0m shows one group at a time. The screen is shorter, but it needs JavaScript to switch groups and
    hides most fields at any moment. It's probably more than 12 fields need.

  For A or B, the groups would use [38;5;153m<fieldset>[39m/[38;5;153m<legend>[39m in [38;5;153msettings.html[39m, so they're also grouped for screen readers. The
  CSS changes would be small. [38;5;153msettings.js[39m wouldn't change because the field names stay the same, so the data sent on
  Save is identical.

  Which layout do you want? You can click one in the browser or reply here. If you'd group the fields differently, say
  so too.

  The mockups are saved under [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/brainstorm/[39m in the repo. There's no [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m yet, so you'll probably want
  to add [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m to one.

